"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2734,"Narrated to us Muhammad ibn [name omitted] al-Basri, who narrated to us Abu al-Junayd, who narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Sa'id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (RA), on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: ""The Black Stone is a white pearl from the pearls of Paradise. It was only blackened by the sins of the polytheists. It will be resurrected on the Day of Judgment the size of Mount Uhud, and it will testify for whoever touched it and kissed it from the people of this world."""
